  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CSB Bank Loan I</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased access to finance for MSMEs, including WMSMEs: IFC anticipates that the proposed investment will help increase access to finance for MSMEs in India, including WMSMEs. 
	Beyond the project level outcomes, IFC anticipates that this investment will promote competitiveness via innovation, demonstration, and replication channels, by encouraging other financial institutions (FIs) to scale up their MSME portfolios, including lending to women borrowers and the agricultural sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed investment consists of a US$ denominated senior loan of up to US$100 million for a tenor of up to 3 years and 3 months to CSB Bank Limited (CSB or the Bank). IFCs investment proceeds will be utilized by CSB for on-lending to Micro, Small and Medium Enterprises (MSMEs), self-employed borrowers (for business/ income generation purposes), women-owned MSMEs (WMSMEs) including self-employed women borrowers, and for providing retail agricultural loans (the Project).</narrative>
  </description>
